{"dur":90,"ev":[{"t":1.2,"type":"voice","id":"v01"},{"t":10.4,"type":"voice","id":"v02"},{"t":25,"type":"voice","id":"v03"},{"t":41,"type":"voice","id":"v04"},{"t":53,"type":"voice","id":"v05"},{"t":63.4,"type":"voice","id":"v06"},{"t":72,"type":"voice","id":"v07"},{"t":84,"type":"voice","id":"v08"},{"t":1.2,"type":"sub","d":5.34,"text":"Rama was a prince of Ayodhya, heir to its throne, and known for keeping his word."},{"t":10.4,"type":"sub","d":8.758,"text":"To keep his father's promise, he gave up the crown and walked into the forest for 14 years, with his wife Sita and his brother Lakshmana."},{"t":25,"type":"sub","d":10.901,"text":"There, a golden deer lured him away, and the demon king Ravana carried Sita off to his island, Lanka. As she flew, she dropped her jewels, to leave a trail."},{"t":41,"type":"sub","d":7.177,"text":"Searching for her, Rama found friends: an army of monkeys, and Hanuman, who leapt across the sea to find her."},{"t":53,"type":"sub","d":5.385,"text":"Then the army built a bridge of floating stones, each one marked with Rama's name."},{"t":63.4,"type":"sub","d":4.298,"text":"In the battle that followed, Ravana fell, and Sita was free at last."},{"t":72,"type":"sub","d":6.415,"text":"When they came home, the people lit their way with lamps. Many still do, every autumn, at Diwali."},{"t":84,"type":"sub","d":2.173,"text":"Rama: the one who kept his word."},{"t":0.1,"type":"brush","d":2.6,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.8,"pan1":0.8},{"t":2.5,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":10.6,"type":"steps","d":9.6},{"t":13,"type":"brush","d":5,"g":0.35},{"t":14.5,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":13,"type":"leaves","d":27},{"t":24.6,"type":"brush","d":1.4,"g":0.3},{"t":26.1,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":26.2,"type":"hooves","d":3.4},{"t":30,"type":"whoosh","d":1.8},{"t":33,"type":"jewels","d":3.2},{"t":39.6,"type":"brush","d":4.4,"g":0.4,"pan0":-0.6,"pan1":0.6},{"t":40.4,"type":"sea","d":31},{"t":42.3,"type":"pencil","d":1},{"t":43,"type":"chatter","d":5},{"t":46.7,"type":"leap","